[Intro — creeping bass, eerie organ]
[Critics — nasal backing whispers]
Look at the donors.
Look at the names.
There must be something
Behind this game.
[Team — low, dry baritone]
The names are public.
The code is too.
But yes, the gnomes
Are coming for you.
[Verse 1]
[Critics]
Who’s giving money?
Where does it go?
What are you funding
That we don’t know?
[Team]
Busted! You caught us.
The secret is out.
We’re funding little laundry thieves
To sneak about.
Boxers, briefs and knickers,
That’s the grand design.
We haven’t worked out step two yet—
But step three’s looking fine.
[Critics — excited]
He said it!
Write it down!
[Team — spoken]
A joke goes in.
A scoop comes out.
[Chorus — low harmonies]
[Team]
Ohmahchi, another build is done.
Back to the keyboard.
Make the computer fun.
[Critics]
We’ve got a theory!
We’ve got a hunch!
[Team]
You and your red string—
What a batty bunch.
You chase a scandal.
We patch and repair.
Your story ends in profits.
Ours is free to share.
[Verse 2]
[Critics]
We’ve put your donors
On the naughty list.
Look at the company
You’re standing with!
[Team]
Better not donate.
Your name might show.
Right beside the others,
All there in a row.
[Critics]
We tried to warn them.
Why won’t they quit?
[Team]
More people chipped in
After reading it.
[Dub break — organ and tape echo]
[Pre-Chorus]
[Critics]
What’s step one?
[Team]
Steal the underwear.
[Critics]
And step two?
[Team]
Still nothing there.
[Critics]
Then how do you—
[Team — beat stops]
PROFIT!
That’s the joke, right there.
[Short Chorus]
[Team]
Ohmahchi, another build is done.
Friends around a keyboard,
Making something run.
[Critics]
There must be more!
[Team]
There’s plenty to repair.
You could send a patch.
Pull up a chair.
[Verse 3]
[Critics]
What mighty machine
Runs this affair?
What have you hidden
Under there?
[Team]
A potato from twenty-twelve.
Four gigs of RAM.
Still a useful computer.
That’s part of the plan.
[Critics]
All this excitement
For that old thing?
[Team]
Watch it come alive.
Hear the old fan sing.
[Bridge — bass only]
[Critics]
Who shipped the update?
Were you awake?
[Team]
I was asleep.
The team was wide awake.
[Critics]
Your people overseas?
Working through the night?
[Team]
Different time zones.
Someone’s got daylight.
[Critics]
And what were they doing?
[Team]
Fixes. Another release.
You’ve found a global team.
You can put down the briefs.
[Verse 4 — guitar returns]
[Critics]
Electronic Confusion.
Another secret name?
[Team]
An old Amiga BBS.
Before this game.
Three nodes humming,
The demoscene.
That feeling coming home
Through a brand-new machine.
People making things,
Showing what they’ve done.
That’s what brought us here.
Computers should be fun.
[Build — critics overlap]
[Critics]
But the money!
And the names!
And the people!
And the claims!
[Team]
Bring a question.
Read the code.
There’s room to help.
A long way to go.
You can keep the yarn
And the missing underwear.
We’ve got something real
To build and share.
[Final Chorus — fuller drums]
[Team]
Ohmahchi, another build is done.
Back to the keyboard.
Make the computer fun.
[Critics]
We’ve got a theory!
We’ve got a hunch!
[Team]
Still drawing arrows?
What a batty bunch.
You chase a scandal.
We patch and repair.
Your story ends in profits.
Ours is free to share.
[Outro — instruments stop]
[Critics — suspicious whisper]
Dave… we’re still asking about step two.
[Team — dry, spoken]
We were hoping you could tell us.
[Silence]
[Critics — triumphant]
So there IS a step two!
[Team — completely dry, exhausted]
Oh, for fuck’s sake.
